{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792705986,"nonce":"10Wr7c7yrstLiZWdta5zu4sCLzA=","title":"zypy: float % differs from CPython in signed-zero results","message":"With and without the float-remainder fast path (ZYNTAX_DISABLE_FREM_FAST_PATH=1), zypy run prints -0.0 for some results CPython prints as 0.0 and omits one -0.0 CPython prints. Reproducer, comparing zypy run against python3:\n\nvals = [7.0, -7.0, 6.0, -6.0, 0.0, 5.5, -5.5, 1e19, float(\"inf\"), float(\"nan\"), 123456789.0, 2.0**53 + 2]\ndivs = [3.0, -3.0, 0.5, 7.0, 1000003.0, float(\"inf\"), 5.0]\nfor v in vals:\n    for d in divs:\n        print(v % d)\n\nPython's % takes the sign of the divisor, so a zero result has the divisor's sign (for example -6.0 % 3.0 is 0.0 and 6.0 % -3.0 is -0.0). The FloorRem lowering (FRem plus a correction) appears to keep the dividend's sign on zero. Not caused by the fast path.","files":null}]}